ics (CBS)).</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec><sec><title>Pre-publication history</title><p>The pre-publication history for this paper can be accessed here:</p><p><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.biomedcentral.com/1471-2296/8/46/prepub"/></p></sec></body><back><ack><sec><title>Acknowledgements</title><p>The Department of General Practice of the Academic Medical Centre covered the expenses made during data collection and analysis. We thank all nurses, GPs, and staff members of the GP cooperative for participating in the study. We also thank Gerben ter Riet, epidemiologist, for assisting on the multivariate adjustment of the differences found between the patient groups within the AED. Finally, the authors would like to express their gratitude to Mildred Beeldman, Marjon van Wingerden, Patrick Jansen and Daan van Schooneveld for their help with the data collection and coding of the problems presented.</p></sec></ack><ref-list><ref id="B1"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hallam</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary medical care outside normal working hours: review of published work</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>1994</year><volume>308</volume><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>253</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8111262</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B2"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Olesen</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Jolleys</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Out of hours service: the Danish solution examined</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>1994</year><volume>309</volume><fpage>1624</fpage><lpage>1626</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7819945</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B3"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van Uden</surname><given-names>CJ